> regard- they hate using English words for things and make their own 
> instead (at least, the official language people do- I can't speak for 
> the actual French themselves).
>
> I honestly think we can describe anything using purely Lojban 
> vocabulary, and further, I think we /should/.
As much as I attempt to avoid using fu'ivla, I doubt that all concepts 
can be reasonably concisely expressed without them, nor am I even 
certain that all can be expressed at all without them.  However, I am 
still a relative novice who has yet to memorize all of the 1,342 gismu.

